From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: riched20: EM_FORMATRANGE; PNG and JPEG pictures; bitmaps and indents saved; zoomed text

What a word processor on RichEdit (sg-shell's WordPad) needed, and every
program that prints or saves through RichEdit with it:

- EM_FORMATRANGE was unsupported, so nothing built on RichEdit could print
  or preview (Wine's own WordPad printed blank pages). It now lays the text
  out for the target device (fr->hdcTarget, else fr->hdc) at the page's
  width, finds the rows from chrg.cpMin that fit fr->rc, draws them on
  fr->hdc (in the target's units when the resolutions differ, so a preview
  measured on a printer is drawn to scale), with the selection hidden and no
  background, restores the screen layout, and returns the first character
  of the next page -- or, when the rest fitted, the text's length + 1 (its
  final paragraph mark) -- and sets rc.bottom to where the text ended, as
  Windows does; the conformance tests' EM_FORMATRANGE expectations (page
  breaks, rc.bottom, return values) now pass and lose their todo_wine.
- \pngblip and \jpegblip pictures (what WordPad and Word write) were
  dropped; they are decoded with OleLoadPicture into a bitmap.
- \dibitmap pictures were read 4 bytes too far (the bits were taken after
  sizeof(BITMAPINFO), which already counts one colour), so every picture's
  colours were shifted; BI_BITFIELDS masks are counted too.
- A picture held as a bitmap was dropped on EM_STREAMOUT (only EMFs were
  written); it is written as \dibitmap0 with its goal size.
- The RTF writer wrote \li as dxOffset and \fi as dxStartIndent, while the
  reader (and RTF) take \li as the left edge of the lines after the first
  and \fi as the first line's offset: indents and hanging lists changed on
  every save.
- A style's Uniscribe cache kept the glyph advances of the font size it was
  made for, so after EM_SETZOOM (or measuring for another device) letters
  overlapped or spread out; it is freed when the style's font height changes.

riched20:editor 10681 tests, 0 failures (the updated tests fail 23 on stock);
richole and txtsrv unchanged.

Gate: sg-shell's test/wordpad-check.sh (printed pages and margins, preview,
pictures' colours and RTF round trip, the ruler's indent in the saved RTF,
the zoomed advance).
